From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: retain old scanout and writeback pins until proved retirement

Reserve old-plane cleanup in the already allocated CRTC state, order the
proof with the actual timer or synchronous flush, and defer video cleanup
past a subsequent vblank. Keep one-shot completion and proved teardown
separate from software counters. A failed proof retains ownership and
refuses another update instead of unpinning potentially active DMA.

The deferred-retirement problem and vblank-work direction were discussed
in Qualcomm's drm/msm KMS SMMU v5 series. This implementation avoids its
cleanup-time allocation fallback and handles the Uke timer-batched tail.

Keep writeback jobs in the DRM queue after timeout, with a device reference,
until actual WB_DONE or successful CTL teardown. Store prepared geometry
per job so preparing a later job cannot replace the active destination.
No board timing, address, firmware or device-tree value is introduced.

Source, fault-injection and native-build evidence do not qualify physical
scanout, controller resets or hot-unplug with active userspace.

Link: https://patchew.org/linux/20261024-fd-kms-fix-smmu-v5-0-a5b0b284aead@oss.qualcomm.com/

